  "summary": "Glitchcore is an aesthetic characterized by the maximalistic use of visual glitches and distortion, incorporating heavily saturated colors, rainbows, flashing patterns, pixelation, and eyestrain.",
  "description": "Glitchcore is an aesthetic characterized by the maximalistic use of visual glitches and distortion, incorporating heavily saturated colors, rainbows, flashing patterns, pixelation, and eyestrain. [ 1 ] It peaked in popularity on TikTok in 2020-2021, [ 2 ] often associated with the Danganronpa fandom. The aesthetic frequently features characters and artwork from cartoons, anime, and video games.\n\nThe term \"Glitchcore\" sometimes also refers to a microgenre of music related to Hyperpop and Digicore. This style is characterized by high-pitched vocals, sharp 808s, frequent hi-hats, and exaggerated use of distortion and glitch effects. Artists like 100 Gecs and Twikipedia are considered pioneers of the Glitchcore music genre. However, it is a common topic of debate on whether it really constitutes a genre. [ 1 ]",
